  "_readme": [
    "Hand-written, first-person notes per water. This file is NEVER written by the scraper or the nightly Action; only edit it by hand.",
    "Keys must match a water name in stocking_data_clean.json exactly (run `python check_notes.py` to verify).",
    "Fields (all optional; blank fields are simply not rendered, and a water with nothing filled in gets no notes block at all):",
    "  access_parking  - how to get there, where to park, fees, gates, road condition.",
    "  shoreline_ramps - shore access, wading, where the ramps are, what condition they are in.",
    "  boats           - one of: none | non_motorized | electric_only | no_wake | unrestricted. Anything else is ignored. Leave blank if unsure; do not guess.",
    "  boats_source    - where the boats rule came from (e.g. 'NM State Parks', 'USFS sign at ramp', 'NMDGF 2026 rules p.42').",
    "  description     - your own observations: what has worked, best season, an honest caveat. Blank line = new paragraph. Plain text only; HTML is escaped.",
    "Keep it to 150-250 words. Photos add more than prose does; add them later via water_images.json."
  ],
